Who gave you permission

268
00:20:42,400 --> 00:20:44,500
to cross the siege line and enter the castle?

269
00:20:44,740 --> 00:20:47,610
Who gave you that sword with the gold lion on the pommel?

270
00:20:47,610 --> 00:20:51,070
Ser Jaime kept his word to your niece Catelyn Stark.

271
00:20:51,780 --> 00:20:54,940
He sent me to find Sansa, to help her as Catelyn wanted.

272
00:20:54,950 --> 00:20:56,930
He gave me this sword to protect her.

273
00:20:56,930 --> 00:20:59,530
That is what I have done and I will continue to do

274
00:20:59,530 --> 00:21:01,410
until the day I die.

275
00:21:15,330 --> 00:21:17,490
She's exactly like her mother.

276
00:21:24,080 --> 00:21:26,930
I don't have enough men to help her take Winterfell.

277
00:21:26,930 --> 00:21:28,960
You have more than she does.

278
00:21:29,070 --> 00:21:31,290
She wants her home back. I understand that.

279
00:21:31,880 --> 00:21:33,410
But this is my home.

280
00:21:33,770 --> 00:21:35,780
And if Jaime Lannister wants it,

281
00:21:35,780 --> 00:21:39,380
he can bloody well take it the way everyone else does.

282
00:21:56,030 --> 00:21:57,310
Find the maester.

283
00:21:59,290 --> 00:22:01,600
We need to get a raven north to Sansa.

284
00:22:03,500 --> 00:22:04,650
What should I write?

285
00:22:08,340 --> 00:22:09,700
Tell her I failed.

286
00:22:40,760 --> 00:22:42,500
There's to be a royal announcement?

287
00:22:43,300 --> 00:22:44,420
There is.

288
00:22:44,490 --> 00:22:45,920
Why wasn't I informed?

289
00:22:48,160 --> 00:22:49,920
There is to be a royal announcement

290
00:22:51,320 --> 00:22:52,750
in the throne room

291
00:22:53,450 --> 00:22:55,120
at this very moment.

292
00:22:58,620 --> 00:22:59,850
Where are you going?

293
00:23:03,520 --> 00:23:05,140
To stand by my son.

294
00:23:05,560 --> 00:23:07,060
Your place is in the gallery

295
00:23:08,240 --> 00:23:10,630
with the other ladies of the court.

296
00:23:18,570 --> 00:23:19,640
Your Grace...

297
00:23:38,250 --> 00:23:40,290
Lords and ladies,

298
00:23:40,820 --> 00:23:43,110
the Faith and the Crown

299
00:23:43,380 --> 00:23:45,590
are the two pillars that hold up this world.

300
00:23:46,830 --> 00:23:50,190
One collapses, so does the other.

301
00:23:51,880 --> 00:23:54,270
The Father judges us all.

302
00:23:54,580 --> 00:23:56,140
If you break his laws...

303
00:23:59,270 --> 00:24:00,550
you will be punished.

304
00:24:03,240 --> 00:24:06,030
After conferring with His Holiness the High Septon,

305
00:24:06,610 --> 00:24:09,070
we have determined that Loras Tyrell

306
00:24:09,070 --> 00:24:10,830
and Cersei Lannister's trial

307
00:24:10,910 --> 00:24:13,160
will be held in the Great Sept of Baelor

308
00:24:13,160 --> 00:24:15,780
on the first day of the Festival of the Mother.

309
00:24:22,100 --> 00:24:26,000
Furthermore, after much prayer and reflection,

310
00:24:27,470 --> 00:24:30,410
the Crown has decided that from this day forward,

311
00:24:30,410 --> 00:24:34,110
trial by combat will be forbidden throughout the Seven Kingdoms.

312
00:24:36,470 --> 00:24:38,210
The tradition is a brutish one,

313
00:24:38,830 --> 00:24:40,670
a scheme devised by corrupt rulers

314
00:24:40,670 --> 00:24:43,470
in order to avoid true judgment from the gods.

315
00:24:43,830 --> 00:24:46,050
Cersei Lannister and Loras Tyrell

316
00:24:46,050 --> 00:24:48,190
will stand trial before seven septons

317
00:24:48,200 --> 00:24:50,580
as it was in the earliest days of the Faith.

318
00:24:51,320 --> 00:24:52,850
Seven blessings to all.

319
00:24:53,510 --> 00:24:55,170
Seven blessings.

320
00:25:17,580 --> 00:25:18,750
Your Grace...

321
00:25:20,750 --> 00:25:23,560
that old rumor you told me about.

322
00:25:25,280 --> 00:25:27,420
My little birds investigated.

323
00:25:29,690 --> 00:25:30,840
And?

324
00:25:32,740 --> 00:25:34,800
Was it just a rumor or something more?

325
00:25:35,990 --> 00:25:37,230
More.

326
00:25:39,450 --> 00:25:40,800
Much more.

327
00:25:47,280 --> 00:25:48,680
You seem happy.

328
00:25:49,560 --> 00:25:50,890
I am happy.

329
00:25:52,470 --> 00:25:54,120
You should both be happy as well.

330
00:25:54,440 --> 00:25:58,460
Not so long ago, this city was ready to devour itself.

331
00:25:58,960 --> 00:26:01,250
Now it's like a man reborn.

332
00:26:01,450 --> 00:26:03,900
I will be happy when our queen returns.

333
00:26:03,940 --> 00:26:07,220
Why don't you drink? Why don't either of you ever drink?

334
00:26:07,220 --> 00:26:08,620
Unsullied never drink.

335
00:26:08,630 --> 00:26:10,000
- Why not? - Rules.

336
00:26:10,000 --> 00:26:11,910
And who made these rules?

337
00:26:12,350 --> 00:26:14,210
Your former masters?

338
00:26:14,880 --> 00:26:18,080
Those miserable old shits didn't want you to be human.

339
00:26:18,150 --> 00:26:19,740
Have a drink with me.

340
00:26:22,790 --> 00:26:26,100
And you? What's your excuse?

341
00:26:26,980 --> 00:26:28,440
I have tried wine before.

342
00:26:28,440 --> 00:26:30,760
It made me feel funny.

343
00:26:30,770 --> 00:26:32,480
That's how you know it's working.

344
00:26:34,910 --> 00:26:36,490
Here's to our queen.

345
00:26:37,900 --> 00:26:40,820
Anyone not drinking is disrespecting our queen.

346
00:26:44,060 --> 00:26:46,380
To Daenerys Stormborn, Mother of Dragons,

347
00:26:46,380 --> 00:26:49,340
Breaker of Chains, long may she reign.

348
00:26:49,340 --> 00:26:51,140
- Long may she reign. - Long may she reign.

349
00:26:57,680 --> 00:26:58,820
Do you like it?

350
00:26:58,820 --> 00:27:00,870
Tastes like it has turned.

351
00:27:00,870 --> 00:27:04,140
Yes, yes. Fermentation.

352
00:27:07,920 --> 00:27:12,310
One day, after our queen has taken the Seven Kingdoms...

353
00:27:14,080 --> 00:27:15,690
I'd like to have my own vineyard.

354
00:27:17,620 --> 00:27:19,030
Make my own wine.

355
00:27:20,570 --> 00:27:22,150
The Imp's Delight.

356
00:27:23,060 --> 00:27:25,430
Only my close friends could drink it.

357
00:27:29,330 --> 00:27:31,340
Tell me a joke, Missandei of Naath.

358
00:27:32,230 --> 00:27:34,180
I do not know any jokes.

359
00:27:34,410 --> 00:27:35,630
Grey Worm?

360
00:27:38,020 --> 00:27:39,160
Right.

361
00:27:41,530 --> 00:27:44,720
Three lords walk into a tavern--

362
00:27:44,870 --> 00:27:47,110
a Stark, a Martell, and a Lannister.

363
00:27:47,110 --> 00:27:48,590
They order ale,

364
00:27:48,800 --> 00:27:51,520
but when the barkeep brings them over,

365
00:27:51,740 --> 00:27:54,470
each of them finds a fly in his cup.

366
00:27:54,480 --> 00:27:56,370
The Lannister, outraged,

367
00:27:56,370 --> 00:27:58,730
shoves the cup aside and demands another.

368
00:27:58,730 --> 00:28:02,930
The Martell plucks the fly out and swallows it whole.

369
00:28:03,650 --> 00:28:06,790
The Stark reaches into his cup,

370
00:28:07,950 --> 00:28:10,180
pulls out the fly and shouts,

371
00:28:10,850 --> 00:28:14,640
"Spit it out, you wee shit. Spit it out."

372
00:28:20,510 --> 00:28:22,300
It's funnier in Westeros.

373
00:28:22,650 --> 00:28:26,020
The Starks and the Lannisters, I thought these were enemies.

374
00:28:26,020 --> 00:28:27,160
Yes.

375
00:28:27,160 --> 00:28:30,380
A joke is like a story, Torgo Nudho.

376
00:28:31,200 --> 00:28:33,140
Not a true story, necessarily.

377
00:28:33,140 --> 00:28:36,240
A story that's supposed to make you laugh ideally.

378
00:28:36,320 --> 00:28:38,110
Not at the moment, perhaps.

379
00:28:38,310 --> 00:28:40,570
Missandei, do you like the wine?

380
00:28:41,060 --> 00:28:42,220
I do.

381
00:28:42,220 --> 00:28:43,600
Tell a joke.

382
00:28:49,860 --> 00:28:52,980
Two translators are on a sinking ship.

383
00:28:53,870 --> 00:28:55,490
The first says,

384
00:28:56,320 --> 00:28:58,120
"Do you know how to swim?"

385
00:28:58,870 --> 00:29:03,120
The second says, "No, but I can shout for help in 19 languages."

386
00:29:12,320 --> 00:29:14,400
That is the worst joke I ever heard.

387
00:29:14,400 --> 00:29:16,120
You don't even know what a joke is.

388
00:29:16,120 --> 00:29:19,390
I am soldier all my life. You think I never hear joke?

389
00:29:19,780 --> 00:29:21,340
You lied to us.

390
00:29:23,250 --> 00:29:24,580
I make joke.

391
00:29:35,370 --> 00:29:36,510
More jokes.

392
00:29:36,770 --> 00:29:40,860
I once walked into a brothel with a honeycomb and a jackass.

393
00:29:40,870 --> 00:29:42,180
The madam says--

394
00:29:55,930 --> 00:29:58,300
The Masters have come for their property.

395
00:30:16,650 --> 00:30:18,050
Lord Edmure.

396
00:30:19,680 --> 00:30:22,160
I apologize for the way the Freys treated you.

397
00:30:22,160 --> 00:30:24,480
A man of your birth deserves better.

398
00:30:24,980 --> 00:30:28,360
You have my word you'll be properly fed and clothed from now on.

399
00:30:30,530 --> 00:30:31,980
I have your word?

400
00:30:34,970 --> 00:30:36,120
Oh, good.

401
00:30:37,330 --> 00:30:38,530
Good, that's--

402
00:30:39,850 --> 00:30:41,190
that's a fine thing.

403
00:30:43,240 --> 00:30:46,160
My uncle will never surrender the castle, ser.

404
00:30:46,420 --> 00:30:48,120
Whatever game you're playing.

405
00:30:48,120 --> 00:30:50,090
The Blackfish is an old man.

406
00:30:50,400 --> 00:30:52,590
A good death is all he can hope for.

407
00:30:52,590 --> 00:30:55,620
But you, you have a child now, I've heard.

408
00:30:56,800 --> 00:30:59,530
A son you sired on your wedding night.

409
00:30:59,780 --> 00:31:01,350
You're a potent man.

410
00:31:01,350 --> 00:31:02,980
A son I've never met

411
00:31:03,840 --> 00:31:06,740
born of a wife that I haven't seen

412
00:31:06,750 --> 00:31:08,180
since our first night together.

413
00:31:08,180 --> 00:31:09,790
You should be with them both.

414
00:31:10,820 --> 00:31:12,970
I can arrange that, you realize?

415
00:31:13,140 --> 00:31:15,660
Comfortable rooms for you at Casterly Rock.

416
00:31:15,660 --> 00:31:17,050
A tutor for your boy,

417
00:31:17,050 --> 00:31:19,000
knights to train him to fight and to ride.

418
00:31:19,000 --> 00:31:21,290
And when he comes of age, he'll have a keep of his own.

419
00:31:21,290 --> 00:31:23,550
Do you imagine yourself a decent person?

420
00:31:24,620 --> 00:31:25,910
Is that it?

421
00:31:26,260 --> 00:31:29,790
After you've massacred my family.

422
00:31:30,990 --> 00:31:33,120
Kept me in a cell for years.

423
00:31:33,120 --> 00:31:34,850
Stolen our lands.

424
00:31:35,170 --> 00:31:37,660
I'll remind you that our houses are at war.

425
00:31:37,660 --> 00:31:40,070
I'm sorry if this conflict has inconvenienced you,

426
00:31:40,070 --> 00:31:42,890
but rebelling against the Crown does have consequences.

427
00:31:42,890 --> 00:31:45,010
Says the man who shoved his sword through his king's back.

428
00:31:45,010 --> 00:31:47,850
Did I give you the impression that this was a negotiation?

429
00:31:47,860 --> 00:31:49,210
It's not.

430
00:31:51,370 --> 00:31:54,120
You understand. On some level you understand

431
00:31:54,510 --> 00:31:56,100
that you're an evil man.

432
00:31:56,390 --> 00:31:58,300
I'll leave the judgments to the gods.

433
00:31:58,300 --> 00:31:59,930
Well, that is convenient for you.

434
00:32:04,080 --> 00:32:07,710
You're a fine-looking fellow, aren't you?

435
00:32:10,280 --> 00:32:11,780
Your square jaw,

436
00:32:12,700 --> 00:32:14,330
your golden armor.

437
00:32:16,230 --> 00:32:19,410
Tell me, I want to know.

438
00:32:19,420 --> 00:32:20,780
I truly do.

439
00:32:20,890 --> 00:32:22,850
How do you live with yourself?

440
00:32:25,860 --> 00:32:28,040
All of us have to believe

441
00:32:28,500 --> 00:32:31,420
that we're decent, don't we?

442
00:32:32,060 --> 00:32:33,660
You have to sleep at night.

443
00:32:35,220 --> 00:32:37,410
How do you tell yourself

444
00:32:37,420 --> 00:32:39,030
that you're decent

445
00:32:39,890 --> 00:32:42,490
after everything that you've done?

446
00:32:48,700 --> 00:32:51,060
I was your sister's prisoner once.

447
00:32:54,250 --> 00:32:57,580
She hit me on the head with a rock if I remember correctly.

448
00:33:00,610 --> 00:33:01,750
Yeah.

449
00:33:03,740 --> 00:33:05,220
She should have killed you.

450
00:33:05,220 --> 00:33:07,090
Perhaps, but she didn't.

451
00:33:08,460 --> 00:33:12,320
Catelyn Stark hated me just like you hate me.

452
00:33:12,570 --> 00:33:14,220
But I didn't hate her.

453
00:33:14,650 --> 00:33:16,240
I admired her.

454
00:33:16,610 --> 00:33:18,560
Far more than her husband or her son.

455
00:33:18,560 --> 00:33:20,720
Do you think I care whom you admire and whom you don't?

456
00:33:20,720 --> 00:33:23,440
No, I don't, but I'm telling you anyway because you're my prisoner.

457
00:33:23,440 --> 00:33:25,050
You don't have a choice.

458
00:33:25,790 --> 00:33:27,560
The love she had for her children,

459
00:33:27,760 --> 00:33:29,500
I was a little awed by it.

460
00:33:29,910 --> 00:33:31,720
Reminded me of my sister.

461
00:33:32,230 --> 00:33:35,440
Oh. Oh, I see.

462
00:33:37,330 --> 00:33:39,050
You're a madman.

463
00:33:39,050 --> 00:33:41,250
I'm not here to trade insults.

464
00:33:41,250 --> 00:33:44,280
- Your sister was a strong-- - Don't talk about Cat!

465
00:33:44,280 --> 00:33:47,180
I'll talk about whomever I want.

466
00:33:48,870 --> 00:33:50,610
She loved her children.

467
00:33:51,270 --> 00:33:53,410
I suppose all mothers do,

468
00:33:53,410 --> 00:33:55,920
but Catelyn and Cersei,

469
00:33:56,310 --> 00:33:58,510
there's a fierceness you don't often see.

470
00:33:58,510 --> 00:34:01,260
They'd do anything to protect their babies.

471
00:34:01,680 --> 00:34:03,270
Start a war.

472
00:34:03,270 --> 00:34:06,540
Burn cities to ash. Free their worst enemies.

473
00:34:07,520 --> 00:34:09,570
The things we do for love.

474
00:34:13,990 --> 00:34:16,840
You didn't come here to talk about our sisters.

475
00:34:17,890 --> 00:34:20,650
That's exactly why I came here.

476
00:34:21,890 --> 00:34:23,830
I love Cersei.

477
00:34:24,950 --> 00:34:26,500
You can laugh at that if you want.

478
00:34:26,500 --> 00:34:28,380
You can sneer. Doesn't matter.

479
00:34:28,770 --> 00:34:30,440
She needs me.

480
00:34:31,010 --> 00:34:34,320
And to get back to her, I have to take Riverrun.

481
00:34:37,770 --> 00:34:39,610
I'll send for your baby boy.

482
00:34:41,280 --> 00:34:44,730
And I'll launch him into Riverrun with a catapult.

483
00:34:45,090 --> 00:34:47,540
Because you don't matter to me, Lord Edmure.

484
00:34:47,920 --> 00:34:50,440
Your son doesn't matter to me.

485
00:34:50,800 --> 00:34:54,400
The people in the castle don't matter to me.

486
00:34:55,360 --> 00:34:57,450
Only Cersei.

487
00:34:59,180 --> 00:35:02,000
And if I have to slaughter every Tully

488
00:35:02,010 --> 00:35:04,340
who ever lived to get back to her,

489
00:35:05,690 --> 00:35:07,220
that's what I'll do.

490
00:35:34,830 --> 00:35:36,350
Who goes there?

491
00:35:37,340 --> 00:35:38,800
Edmure Tully,

492
00:35:38,800 --> 00:35:40,480
son of Hoster Tully

493
00:35:40,480 --> 00:35:42,750
and the rightful Lord of Riverrun.

494
00:35:45,590 --> 00:35:47,340
I demand entry.

495
00:35:48,020 --> 00:35:49,530
Don't let him in.

496
00:35:51,100 --> 00:35:52,740
He's the Lord of Riverrun.

497
00:35:52,740 --> 00:35:54,140
I have to obey his commands.

498
00:35:54,140 --> 00:35:55,630
He's been their captive

499
00:35:55,630 --> 00:35:58,430
ever since they murdered his king at the Red Wedding.

500
00:35:58,700 --> 00:36:01,710
Why do you think the people who murdered his king at the Red Wedding

501
00:36:01,710 --> 00:36:04,160
would decide to let him come home?

502
00:36:05,330 --> 00:36:07,600
Because it's a trap, you idiot.

503
00:36:08,580 --> 00:36:09,950
Don't let him in.

504
00:36:09,950 --> 00:36:11,390
He's my lord, my lord.

505
00:36:11,400 --> 00:36:14,420
I've sworn to serve the Lord of Riverrun and obey his commands.

506
00:36:14,420 --> 00:36:17,390
You're not obeying Edmure's commands.

507
00:36:17,570 --> 00:36:21,060
You're obeying the fucking Kingslayer's commands.

508
00:36:21,580 --> 00:36:23,270
I demand entry.

509
00:36:24,260 --> 00:36:25,670
My lord has given an order.

510
00:36:25,680 --> 00:36:27,660
With a knife to his throat.

511
00:36:27,660 --> 00:36:30,080
That is not a valid order.

512
00:36:35,050 --> 00:36:37,000
Lower the drawbridge and open the gate for Lord Ed...

513
00:36:37,010 --> 00:36:37,920
Aye, ser.

514
00:36:39,210 --> 00:36:43,160
I'll have your head before I surrender Riverrun.

515
00:36:43,170 --> 00:36:46,960
You are not lord of this castle, my lord.

516
00:36:58,480 --> 00:37:01,140
- Lower the drawbridge. - Aye, ser!

517
00:37:45,850 --> 00:37:47,450
If you're wrong,

518
00:37:48,280 --> 00:37:51,250
we've just surrendered our most valuable prisoner.

519
00:38:31,090 --> 00:38:32,750
Welcome home, my lord.

520
00:38:37,860 --> 00:38:41,230
Command all the forces within the castle to lay down their arms.

521
00:38:43,450 --> 00:38:44,870
Open the gates.

522
00:38:45,140 --> 00:38:47,540
- My lord... - Your lord has given a command.

523
00:39:21,770 --> 00:39:24,600
Infantry, advance!

524
00:39:38,030 --> 00:39:39,720
Find the Blackfish.

525
00:39:40,990 --> 00:39:44,040
Put him in irons and hand him over to the Freys.

526
00:39:48,370 --> 00:39:49,510
Find him.

527
00:40:14,560 --> 00:40:15,740
Go on.

528
00:40:16,850 --> 00:40:17,990
Come with us.

529
00:40:17,990 --> 00:40:19,950
I've run before from the Red Wedding.

530
00:40:19,950 --> 00:40:22,260
I'm not running again. This is my family home.

531
00:40:22,260 --> 00:40:26,010
Your family is in the North. Come with us.

532
00:40:26,150 --> 00:40:29,090
Don't die for pride when you can fight for your blood.

533
00:40:30,590 --> 00:40:34,390
You'll serve Sansa far better than I ever could.

534
00:40:39,340 --> 00:40:40,900
All the way down!

535
00:40:40,900 --> 00:40:42,720
- Check that out! - Go on, now.

536
00:40:43,890 --> 00:40:46,690
I haven't had a proper sword fight in years.

537
00:40:47,140 --> 00:40:49,720
I expect I'll make a damn fool of myself.

538
00:41:23,990 --> 00:41:26,080
We found the Blackfish, my lord.

539
00:41:26,900 --> 00:41:27,900
Good.

540
00:41:28,190 --> 00:41:29,410
Bring him to me.

541
00:41:30,770 --> 00:41:33,260
He died fighting, my lord.

542
00:43:03,330 --> 00:43:05,800
- I was wrong. I admit it. - That changes nothing.

543
00:43:05,800 --> 00:43:08,060
The Unsullied could mount a defense off the beachhead.

544
00:43:08,060 --> 00:43:10,070
- If the slavers' forces-- - No more talking from you.

545
00:43:10,070 --> 00:43:11,370
Your talking gave us this.

546
00:43:11,370 --> 00:43:13,080
And I have acknowledged that. I'm trying--

547
00:43:13,080 --> 00:43:14,710
You're trying to tell me what the army should do.

548
00:43:14,710 --> 00:43:16,520
You do not know what the army should do.

549
00:43:17,430 --> 00:43:19,720
All right, what should the army do?

550
00:43:19,910 --> 00:43:21,560
We'll not go to the beach.

551
00:43:21,830 --> 00:43:24,300
If we go to the beach, the Masters will take the pyramid.

552
00:43:24,300 --> 00:43:26,470
The pyramid is the only place in the city we can defend.

553
00:43:26,470 --> 00:43:28,150
- We stay here. - And then?

554
00:43:28,160 --> 00:43:29,820
We wait for them to come to us.

555
00:43:29,860 --> 00:43:31,150
Then we fight them.

556
00:44:42,380 --> 00:44:43,650
Clegane.

557
00:44:44,150 --> 00:44:46,060
What the fuck you doing here?

558
00:44:46,060 --> 00:44:48,600
Chasing them. You?

559
00:44:48,600 --> 00:44:49,940
Hanging them.

560
00:44:50,530 --> 00:44:52,250
Any particular reason?

561
00:44:52,250 --> 00:44:54,500
They're our men. Or they were.

562
00:44:54,720 --> 00:44:57,530
They attacked a nearby sept and murdered the villagers.

563
00:44:57,620 --> 00:44:58,700
Why do you want them?

564
00:44:58,700 --> 00:45:00,130
Same reason.

565
00:45:00,250 --> 00:45:01,940
I was helping build it.

566
00:45:02,860 --> 00:45:04,520
They killed a friend of mine.

567
00:45:04,790 --> 00:45:05,920
You've got friends?

568
00:45:06,410 --> 00:45:09,110
Not anymore. They're mine.

569
00:45:09,360 --> 00:45:11,650
It's the Brotherhood's good name they've dragged through the dirt.

570
00:45:11,650 --> 00:45:13,400
Fuck your name. They're mine.

571
00:45:13,400 --> 00:45:14,990
I killed you once before, Dondarrion.

572
00:45:14,990 --> 00:45:16,200
Happy to do it again.

573
00:45:17,190 --> 00:45:18,990
Drop that arrow, you bloody girl.

574
00:45:20,840 --> 00:45:23,050
Tougher girls than you have tried to kill me.

575
00:45:25,670 --> 00:45:26,760
You can have one of them.

576
00:45:31,980 --> 00:45:32,850
Two.

577
00:45:44,870 --> 00:45:46,590
No, no, no.

578
00:45:47,220 --> 00:45:49,590
We're not butchers. We hang them.

579
00:45:49,590 --> 00:45:50,470
Hanging?

580
00:45:51,230 --> 00:45:52,920
All over in an instant.

581
00:45:52,920 --> 00:45:54,470
Where's the punishment in that?

582
00:45:54,470 --> 00:45:56,860
- They die. - We all bloody die.

583
00:45:56,870 --> 00:45:58,260
Except this one here.

584
00:46:00,020 --> 00:46:01,470
I'll only gut one of them.

585
00:46:01,620 --> 00:46:02,380
No.

586
00:46:04,450 --> 00:46:05,890
I'll chop off one hand.

587
00:46:06,000 --> 00:46:09,060
We gave you two of the three out of respect for your loss.

588
00:46:09,370 --> 00:46:10,490
That's generous.

589
00:46:14,780 --> 00:46:16,390
Bunch of nancies.

590
00:46:18,070 --> 00:46:20,080
There was a time I would have killed all seven of you

591
00:46:20,080 --> 00:46:21,470
just to gut these three.

592
00:46:21,470 --> 00:46:23,090
You're getting old, Clegane.

593
00:46:23,340 --> 00:46:24,340
He's not.

594
00:46:27,040 --> 00:46:29,400
Please don't. I'll give you anything.

595
00:46:57,730 --> 00:46:59,080
Got anything to eat?

596
00:47:11,850 --> 00:47:13,070
Enjoying yourself?

597
00:47:14,490 --> 00:47:15,840
I prefer chicken.

598
00:47:17,720 --> 00:47:20,990
You ought to join us. We could use you.

599
00:47:21,940 --> 00:47:24,660
I tried joining. Didn't work out for me.

600
00:47:24,660 --> 00:47:27,270
Clegane, we're here for a reason.

601
00:47:29,500 --> 00:47:32,690
The Lord of Light is keeping Beric alive for a reason.

602
00:47:32,940 --> 00:47:35,180
He gave a failed, drunk priest

603
00:47:35,190 --> 00:47:37,790
the power to bring him back for a reason.

604
00:47:38,250 --> 00:47:40,900
We are part of something larger than ourselves.

605
00:47:41,460 --> 00:47:43,610
Lots of horrible shit in this world gets done

606
00:47:43,610 --> 00:47:45,900
for something larger than ourselves.

607
00:47:53,580 --> 00:47:55,610
Cold winds are rising in the North.

608
00:47:55,950 --> 00:47:57,870
And you're going to go stop them?

609
00:47:59,600 --> 00:48:01,220
We need good men to help us.

610
00:48:02,210 --> 00:48:04,990
Last time you saw me, you wanted to execute me.

611
00:48:06,670 --> 00:48:07,650
True enough.

612
00:48:08,510 --> 00:48:11,210
But the Lord of Light gave you the power to defeat me.

613
00:48:11,940 --> 00:48:12,740
Why?

614
00:48:13,900 --> 00:48:16,500
I beat you because I'm better than you, Beric.

615
00:48:17,520 --> 00:48:18,640
I was better than you

616
00:48:18,640 --> 00:48:21,250
before you started yammering on about the Lord

617
00:48:21,720 --> 00:48:23,640
and I'm better than you now.

618
00:48:24,570 --> 00:48:26,210
Aye, you're probably right.

619
00:48:27,290 --> 00:48:28,340
You're a fighter.

620
00:48:29,410 --> 00:48:31,330
You were born a fighter.

621
00:48:31,980 --> 00:48:33,670
You walked away from the fight.

622
00:48:34,500 --> 00:48:35,670
How did that go?

623
00:48:39,000 --> 00:48:41,570
Good and bad, young and old,

624
00:48:42,370 --> 00:48:45,100
the things we're fighting will destroy them all alike.

625
00:48:46,630 --> 00:48:49,950
You can still help a lot more than you've harmed, Clegane.

626
00:48:50,310 --> 00:48:51,730
It's not too late for you.

627
00:49:55,780 --> 00:49:56,810
Lady Crane?

628
00:50:05,760 --> 00:50:06,870
Lady Crane?

629
00:50:14,170 --> 00:50:17,890
If you'd have done your job, she would have died painlessly.

630
00:50:20,150 --> 00:50:21,100
Instead...

631
00:50:24,260 --> 00:50:26,360
The Many-Faced God was promised a name.

632
00:50:27,930 --> 00:50:30,130
He must always receive what is his.

633
00:50:30,730 --> 00:50:32,430
You can't change that.

634
00:50:33,690 --> 00:50:35,170
I can't change that.

635
00:50:35,880 --> 00:50:37,120
No one can.

636
00:50:40,360 --> 00:50:42,480
And now he's been promised another name.

637
00:50:58,420 --> 00:51:00,200
- Hey! - Get out!

638
00:52:45,770 --> 00:52:47,390
My basket!

639
00:54:22,100 --> 00:54:23,720
It will all be over soon.

640
00:54:25,080 --> 00:54:27,980
On your knees or on your feet?

641
00:54:38,970 --> 00:54:40,760
Haven't we been through this already?

642
00:54:42,810 --> 00:54:44,390
That won't help you.

643
00:55:56,620 --> 00:55:58,140
You told her to kill me.

644
00:56:05,800 --> 00:56:06,670
Yes.

645
00:56:07,810 --> 00:56:08,950
But here you are.

646
00:56:10,570 --> 00:56:12,110
And there she is.

647
00:56:22,770 --> 00:56:24,990
Finally a girl is no one.

648
00:56:28,980 --> 00:56:31,470
A girl is Arya Stark of Winterfell

649
00:56:32,710 --> 00:56:34,370
and I'm going home.

